                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba328182-6818-3521-ae68-680ce49cc7d7",
                                        "entry_id": "40c37f79-eeac-328a-8c66-84c7b5d14cde",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An open structure of light material set upon a roof, to give light and air to the interior."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5009da2d-fbe0-440f-b76c-b4df489e3e61",
                                                "sense_id": "ba328182-6818-3521-ae68-680ce49cc7d7",
                                                "text": "On such an afternoon, if ever, the Lord High Chancellor ought to be sitting here—as here he is—with a foggy glory round his head, softly fenced in with crimson cloth and curtains, addressed by a large advocate with great whiskers, a little voice, and an interminable brief, and outwardly directing his contemplation to the lantern in the roof, where he can see nothing but fog."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33076e1a-59fe-40d0-9475-d50af892d2bf",
                                                "sense_id": "ba328182-6818-3521-ae68-680ce49cc7d7",
                                                "text": "The station also boasts a large semi-domed French pavilion roof with fish-scale tiles and iron cresting, plus a rectangular hall with arcaded upper storey and wooden lantern."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a172d408-a223-3020-9690-c54cf7058760",
                                        "entry_id": "40c37f79-eeac-328a-8c66-84c7b5d14cde",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cage or open chamber of rich architecture, open below into the building or tower which it crowns."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d13619b5-2aab-3298-be01-c7cf556f83e3",
                                        "entry_id": "40c37f79-eeac-328a-8c66-84c7b5d14cde",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A smaller and secondary cupola crowning a larger one, for ornament, or to admit light."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c099b7e9-e2b9-4fc2-b4c2-ae0e2b8ed8d2",
                                                "sense_id": "d13619b5-2aab-3298-be01-c7cf556f83e3",
